Win rate: 33.3% — well below the 37.5% needed to break even with the current 1.43:1 reward/risk ratio.

Root Cause #1 — BB_SQUEEZE Monopoly (196/214 bots)
The trio of strategies is heavily skewed. Looking at the recommendation logic at pair_scanner.py:118-144: recommend_strategy() votes by confidence score. BB_SQUEEZE consistently scores 0.75–0.85, while VWAP_RSI scores 0.46–0.68 and EMA_CROSS rarely triggers at all.

The problem: BB_SQUEEZE confidence is artificially inflated. At scalping_strategies.py:270-273:


if breakout_up and macd_bull and trend_up and trend_strong:
    confidence = 0.60 + (0.15 if macd_bull else 0) + (0.10 if adx_val > 25 else 0)
The base confidence starts at 0.60 and only goes up. Conditions are binary (macd_bull is always True since the if already checks it), so confidence is always 0.75–0.85. Meanwhile, EMA_CROSS at scalping_strategies.py:182-186 starts at 0.55 — BB_SQUEEZE always wins the vote even when EMA_CROSS is objectively better for trending markets.

Root Cause #2 — SL Too Tight for 5m Noise
At scalping_strategies.py:40-48: SL = price ± atr * 1.5, TP = price ± atr * 2.5.

On 5-minute candles, ATR is ~0.30–0.50% of price. So:

SL distance: 0.45–0.75% from entry
TP distance: 0.75–1.25% from entry
At 0.45% SL, the stop is barely beyond the bid-ask spread + one tick of noise. A random wick in a 5m candle will hit SL before the price has a chance to reach TP. This explains the 67% loss rate — most entries get stopped out by normal volatility, not by being directionally wrong.

Root Cause #3 — BB_SQUEEZE False Breakouts on 5m
The strategy at scalping_strategies.py:238-247 requires:

Previous candle BB width was in the 20th percentile (squeeze)
Current candle closes outside the band (breakout)
On 5m charts, BB squeeze breakouts are notoriously unreliable — about 60-70% are false. The band expansion after a squeeze means the candle wick pierces the band, the strategy enters, and then price reverses back inside. By the time the entry is confirmed at candle close, the move is already exhausted.

Root Cause #4 — Sell-Side Bias Against Market Trend
165 of 336 trades are SELL (49%), but in a generally up-trending crypto market, short scalps get crushed. The BB_SQUEEZE's breakout_down fires more frequently because downward moves are sharper (panic selling creates cleaner breakouts) — but they also reverse faster.

Root Cause #5 — Auto-Pilot TP Multiplier Mismatch
At pair_scanner.py:356-368, auto-created bots use tp_atr_mult=2.5 hardcoded. But the strategy code comments say "TP reducido a 2.0× ATR" at scalping_strategies.py:208. The higher TP target makes it harder to hit before SL does.

Recommended Strategy Fixes
Fix 1 — Widen SL, Tighten TP
In save_scan_results pair_scanner.py:364-365, change auto-pilot bot params:


# Current:
sl_atr_mult=1.5,
tp_atr_mult=2.5,
# Fix:
sl_atr_mult=2.2,  # Wider SL avoids noise
tp_atr_mult=1.6,  # Achievable TP, 1:1.4 risk/reward
This gives SL 0.7–1.1% from entry and TP 0.5–0.8%. With a tighter TP, the win rate should increase significantly. A 55% win rate at 1:1.4 is profitable.

Fix 2 — Normalize Confidence Scores
At scalping_strategies.py:186 and scalping_strategies.py:274, set maximum 0.75 for BB_SQUEEZE and boost EMA_CROSS to 0.70 base:


# BB_SQUEEZE: cap confidence
confidence = min(0.60 + bonus, 0.75)
# EMA_CROSS: raise base
confidence = 0.65 + bonus  # was 0.55
Fix 3 — Add Volume Filter to BB_SQUEEZE Entry
At scalping_strategies.py:270, add and vol_ok (breakout volume > 1.5x average). False breakouts nearly always have low volume.

Fix 4 — Add Cooldown After SL Hit
In run_scalping_bot_task tasks.py:378-498, after a CLOSED_SL, set a 5-candle cooldown before re-entering. Currently, bots can re-enter immediately on the next candle and get stopped again.

Fix 5 — Reduce BB_SQUEEZE Dominance in Scanner
In recommend_strategy pair_scanner.py:118-144, when ADX > 25, enforce EMA_CROSS over BB_SQUEEZE regardless of confidence votes. Trending markets favor momentum strategies, not squeeze breakout.

